    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did the city of Troy really exist? For a long time, many people thought it was just a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "myth",
            "ref": "v-myth"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But Heinrich Schliemann, a German businessman, believed otherwise. His belief led him to make some very important discoveries."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As a child, Schliemann loved to read. His favourite book was "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "The Iliad"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "《伊利亚特》"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The stories of brave heroes fighting in front of Troy’s giant walls interested him deeply. As he grew older, he made a promise to himself: If he ever had a chance, he would find the lost city of Troy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, after finishing school, Schliemann didn’t become a historian. Instead, he jumped into the world of business. His jobs took him to many different places around the world and earned him a lot of money. Along the way, Schliemann also picked up several languages, including English, French, Spanish, Italian, and Russian."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "By his late forties, Schliemann had enough money to finally follow his childhood dream. He travelled through Greece and Turkey, searching for Troy. Hissarlik, an ancient Turkish site, caught his eye."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In 1871, Schliemann began digging at Hissarlik. He didn’t work alone; he hired a team of local workers. However, the work "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "progressed",
            "ref": "v-progress"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " slowly. Schliemann grew "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "impatient",
            "ref": "v-impatient"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and bought boxes of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "dynamite",
            "zh": "炸药"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". These explosives sped up the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "excavation",
            "zh": "挖掘"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " but also caused serious damage to the site."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Piece by piece, Schliemann and his team "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "uncovered",
            "ref": "v-uncover"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " weapons, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pottery",
            "zh": "陶器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and many other ancient objects. These findings showed that Hissarlik had a history of over 5,000 years. It had been built, destroyed, and rebuilt at least seven times. One of these cities, Schliemann believed, was Troy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Schliemann’s findings brought him international fame. But not all historians think highly of him. His decision to use explosives at Hissarlik is considered "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "unforgivable",
            "ref": "v-unforgivable"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", as many priceless artifacts were lost due to his impatience."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
